  "question": {
    "text": "If non-zero real numbers&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> are such that&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>;&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lies in the interval&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
